br/>As you are now, so once was I,<br /> As I am now, so you will be.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/285-andonno","name":"Andonno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:47:37-07:00","id":282665,"title":"","content":"Inspirational music thread, I summon you! Rise from your grave to rescue my daughter!<br /> <br /> Mind you, this is a bit of a cheat. While the music is a driving techno beat suitable for Demon, the real highlight here is the music video. Warnings: mild robot nudity, extreme violence, epilepsy-very-unsafe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t6maVVFs0As\" data-code=\"t6maVVFs0As\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/t6maVVFs0As/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I don't remember where I discovered Ken Ishii through the music video for his 1995 track Extra, above, and I suspect it was from some thread on these forums, really, but I double-checked to make sure it wasn't this thread in particular. This is an abstract animated short by the director of Akira, and it shows; it's a cyberpunk fever-dream suitable for especially nihilistic, grungy or futuristic games of Demon in particular. Society grows wild and decadent; people wear paper bags over their heads and become faceless; technology is exploitative and abusive behind a facade of excess; rogue machines run rampant and predatory for unclear reasons and yet end up seeming the lesser threat; none of these are new ideas (and they show some nineties fearful exaggeration similar in tone to the Classic World of Darkness if that's your thing), but the visuals are fantastically realized.<br /> <br /> In an oddly fitting way, while some of the designs seem suitable inspiration for angelic and demonic forms, the figures in the video that remind me the most of the Unchained are the most ordinary, relatable human figures. The girl on the tricycle and the boy in the goggles are placed in roles that seem to oppose the wild predation of the setting, but they seem to be serving their own goals rather than straightforward self-preservation or banding together; they're free agents who seem safer to be around for any hypothetical bystanders, but not any less dangerous in their own ways. Questions of identity emerge; they might all be the same person, or at least, it seems heavily implied that the girl is not just a little girl but a facade hiding an armed and skilled &quot;player.&quot;<br /> <br /> Take what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:43:49-07:00","id":287832,"title":"","content":"After reading Heirs to Hell, I think that The Pretender by Foo Fighters makes a pretty good song for an Offspring or Fractal, talking to an Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T06:41:08-07:00","id":298899,"title":"","content":"integrator theme- Feathery Wings by Voltaire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T22:00:46-08:00","id":315079,"title":"","content":"There's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QGhUfhQ-_PI\" target=\"_blank\">the first/titular track from the Psycho-Pass OST</a>, or, as I like to think of it, &quot;the climactic chase scene BGM.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:13:44-08:00","id":315607,"title":"","content":"This isn't quite inspirational music, but it falls under the same idea. When I ran <b>Demon</b>, I really wanted the tone to be different from other WoD games I've run. Usually I use film noir-esque music to evoke a mood, but I thought that wasn't quite right. I ended up getting the most recent Boards of Canada album, <i>Tomorrow's Harvest</i>, which is normally not my thing. It's all instrumental, but very evocative of the &quot;techgnostic&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> Here's a standout:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwz9Ue4RH-w\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwz9Ue4RH-w\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwz9Ue4RH-w </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwz9Ue4RH-w\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwz9Ue4RH-w </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2